  "@type": "Recipe",
  "recipeCuisine": "Indonesia",
  "name": "Nasi Goreng",
  "text": "Nasi Goreng\n\nYield: 2\n\nPreparation time: 10 minutes\n\nCooking time: 30 minutes\n\nIngredients\n\nFor the spice paste\n\n1 peeled garlic cloves,\n\ntiny pinch nutmeg,\n\ngood pinch freshly ground black pepper,\n\n1/4 tsp ground turmeric,\n\n1 peeled shallots,\n\n20 g unsalted peanuts,\n\n1/2 tsp salt,\n\n1 birds'-eye chilli (deseeded),\n\n1/2 tbsp palm sugar,\n\n1/2-1 tbsp vegetable oil (or more if necessary),\n\nFor the stir-fry\n\n1 tbsp vegetable or groundnut oil (plus extra for frying the eggs),\n\n1 chicken breasts (skin removed and cut into thin strips),\n\n120 g prawns (heads and shells removed and de-veined),\n\n60 g fine green beans (trimmed and sliced into 1cm pieces),\n\n2 spring onions (sliced),\n\n120 g cooked long-grain rice (this must be cold),\n\nsplash light soy sauce,\n\nsplash ketjap manis,\n\n2 eggs,\n\nFor the garnish\n\n1/4 cucumber (peeled, seeds removed, finely diced),\n\n1/2 tbsp roughly chopped coriander,\n\n25g peanuts,\n\n1/2 lime cut into wedges,\n\nhandful crispy fried shallots,\n\nAsian-style chilli oil to serve.\n\nPreparation\n\n1. Spice Paste\n\n1.1 Put the peanuts in the chopper/grinder and grind until all the large pieces have broken down.\n\n1.2 Add all the other ingredients except the oil and chop until slightly lump paste.\n\n1.3 Add the oil and blend to a smooth paste.\n\n2. Garnish\n\n2.1 Chop the cucumber in half and remove the seeds with a spoon.\n\n2.2 Roughly crush the peanuts in a pestle and mortar.\n\n3. Crispy shallots\n\n3.1 Heat the oil in the wok and fry two finely chopped shallots until crispy.\n\n3.2 Put on a paper towel to remove the oil, then set aside.\n\n4. Fried egg\n\n4.1 Fry each egg in the oil and set aside somewhere warm.\n\n5. Stir Fry\n\n5.1. Heat the oil in a wok over a high heat until shimmering\n\nhot, then add the chicken and fry for a minute or so.\n\n5.2 Add the spice paste and prawns and stir well, cooking for a good 4-5 minutes.\n\n5.3 Add the beans and spring onions and fry for another minute, keeping everything moving.\n\n5.4. Add the cooked rice and stir until it's all been incorporated (add a few tablespoons of water at this point if it becomes dry and starts to stick).\n\n5.5 Season with soy sauce and ketjap manis, to taste.\n\n5.6 Using a spare bowl form each portion by pressing the rice into the bowl and poping out onto a plate.\n\n5.7 Put the fried egg on the top.\n\n5.8 Put the cucumber and crushed peanuts on the side.\n\n5.9 Drizzle a little chilli oil over the top.",
  "recipeYield": "2",
  "prepTime": "PT10M",
  "cookTime": "PT30M",
